BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Steadyhand Grips) Tj T* () Tj T* (STEADYHAND GRIPS) Tj T* (Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Millions of Americans live with arthritis, essential tremor, Parkinsons and other conditions) Tj T* (that effect there hands. For these people everyday tasks like stirring a pot, using a peeler or) Tj T* (pruning roses becomes painful and sometimes impossible. This loss of ability is not just a) Tj T* (physical problem it is a emotional one as well, because cooking and gardening are things that) Tj T* (give people a sense of purpose and independance. When they can no longer do them they often) Tj T* (have to rely on family members or caregivers which impacts quality of life in a big way. We) Tj T* (believe this is a significant problem that is not being addressed properly in todays market.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Steadyhand Grips is a custom solution that addresses this problem head on. We take a mold of) Tj T* (each customers hand using a safe moldable material, and then we create a grip made to fit that) Tj T* (exact hand which attaches to the persons existing utensils and tools. Because every hand is) Tj T* (different, and every condition is different, our approach is personal and tailored rather than) Tj T* (one size fits all. The grip is made from durable materials that is comfortable and easy to) Tj T* (clean. Along with the grip we provide a fitting service, where one of our team members works) Tj T* (with the customer to make sure the grip is right and adjust it if needed. This combination of a) Tj T* (physical product and a personal service is what makes Steadyhand unique and gives customers a) Tj T* (feeling of being cared for.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The market for our product is very large. According to our research there are tens of millions) Tj T* (of adults in the United States with some form of arthritis and many more with other hand) Tj T* (conditions, and this number is growing every year as the population gets older. Baby boomers) Tj T* (are retiring and want to stay active and independant for as long as possible. If even a small) Tj T* (percentage of these people were to purchase our grips this would be a multi million dollar) Tj T* (opportunity. We also believe there is potential in related markets such as occupational) Tj T* (therapy, assisted living facilities, and eventually the general consumer market for ergonomic) Tj T* (tools. The adaptive products space is expanding rapidly and we are positioned to take advantage) Tj T* (of this trend.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our business model is based on selling custom grips along with the fitting service. Customers) Tj T* (would pay for the fitting and the grip together, and we may also offer additional grips for) Tj T* (other tools at a lower price. We are still determining our exact pricing but we are looking at) Tj T* (somewhere between a fair price that customers can afford and a price that allows us to be) Tj T* (profitable. In the future we may also explore subscription options, partnerships with) Tj T* (therapists and clinics, and selling through retail channels. We think there are many different) Tj T* (ways to generate revenue and we will figure out which is best as we grow and learn more about) Tj T* (our customers needs. Our costs will include materials, molding supplies, labor for the) Tj T* (fittings, and marketing.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are existing companies that sell adaptive kitchen tools and ergonomic grips, and some of) Tj T* (them have been around for a long time. However we believe that our product is different because) Tj T* (it is truly custom and comes with a personal service. Most of the competition sells standard) Tj T* (sized foam handles or thick utensils that dont fit everyone. Some people also make there own) Tj T* (grips at home using tape or putty. We believe our customers will pay more for something that is) Tj T* (made for them specifically. We also think that our team is more passionate and more agile then) Tj T* (larger companies who may be slow to respond to customer feedback. Our personal approach is) Tj ET
